Column name: potential usage  
• "path": location of each file; used to ① identify the file‑name extension (.py, .c, .ipynb, .java, .js) and ② measure directory depth by counting “/”.  
• "repo_name": optional filter in case we want to restrict to particular repositories (not strictly needed for the task).  
• Other columns ("mode", "id", "ref", "symlink_target") are not essential to count file‑types vs. depth.

Conditions that may be used  
• Directory depth > 10 →  ( LENGTH("path")‑LENGTH(REPLACE("path", '/', '')) ) > 10  
• Extension match →  "path" ILIKE '%.py'  (similar for .c, .ipynb, .java, .js)

Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL queries (each ends with LIMIT 20) growing from simple inspection to a final aggregation that could answer the original question.

```sql
-- Description: 1) Quick look at a handful of file paths in the sample to understand the data.
SELECT 
  "repo_name",
  "path"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_FILES"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 2) Show distinct file‑name extensions that exist in the sample.
SELECT DISTINCT
  SPLIT_PART("path", '.', -1) AS "extension"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_FILES"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 3) For a few rows, display directory depth (slash count) beside each path.
SELECT 
  "path",
  ( LENGTH("path") - LENGTH(REPLACE("path", '/', '')) )  AS "dir_depth"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_FILES"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 4) Peek at Python files whose directory depth is already > 10.
SELECT 
  "path"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_FILES"
WHERE "path" ILIKE '%.py'
  AND ( LENGTH("path") - LENGTH(REPLACE("path", '/', '')) ) > 10
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 5) Same preview for C source files.
SELECT 
  "path"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_FILES"
WHERE "path" ILIKE '%.c'
  AND ( LENGTH("path") - LENGTH(REPLACE("path", '/', '')) ) > 10
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 6) Preview Jupyter notebooks (.ipynb) at depth > 10.
SELECT 
  "path"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_FILES"
WHERE "path" ILIKE '%.ipynb'
  AND ( LENGTH("path") - LENGTH(REPLACE("path", '/', '')) ) > 10
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 7) Preview Java source files at depth > 10.
SELECT 
  "path"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_FILES"
WHERE "path" ILIKE '%.java'
  AND ( LENGTH("path") - LENGTH(REPLACE("path", '/', '')) ) > 10
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 8) Preview JavaScript files at depth > 10.
SELECT 
  "path"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_FILES"
WHERE "path" ILIKE '%.js'
  AND ( LENGTH("path") - LENGTH(REPLACE("path", '/', '')) ) > 10
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 9) Count how many files for each of the five requested extensions
-- have directory depth > 10.  This gives numeric results suitable for comparison.
SELECT 
  CASE
    WHEN "path" ILIKE '%.py'   THEN '.py'
    WHEN "path" ILIKE '%.c'    THEN '.c'
    WHEN "path" ILIKE '%.ipynb' THEN '.ipynb'
    WHEN "path" ILIKE '%.java' THEN '.java'
    WHEN "path" ILIKE '%.js'   THEN '.js'
  END                          AS "file_type",
  COUNT(*)                     AS "file_count"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_FILES"
WHERE ( LENGTH("path") - LENGTH(REPLACE("path", '/', '')) ) > 10
  AND (
        "path" ILIKE '%.py' OR
        "path" ILIKE '%.c' OR
        "path" ILIKE '%.ipynb' OR
        "path" ILIKE '%.java' OR
        "path" ILIKE '%.js'
      )
GROUP BY "file_type"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 10) Identify which of the five extensions has the maximum count
-- when directory depth > 10 (ties ignored).  This answers the question directly.
SELECT *
FROM (
  SELECT 
    CASE
      WHEN "path" ILIKE '%.py'   THEN '.py'
      WHEN "path" ILIKE '%.c'    THEN '.c'
      WHEN "path" ILIKE '%.ipynb' THEN '.ipynb'
      WHEN "path" ILIKE '%.java' THEN '.java'
      WHEN "path" ILIKE '%.js'   THEN '.js'
    END                          AS "file_type",
    COUNT(*)                     AS "file_count"
  FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_FILES"
  WHERE ( LENGTH("path") - LENGTH(REPLACE("path", '/', '')) ) > 10
    AND (
          "path" ILIKE '%.py' OR
          "path" ILIKE '%.c' OR
          "path" ILIKE '%.ipynb' OR
          "path" ILIKE '%.java' OR
          "path" ILIKE '%.js'
        )
  GROUP BY "file_type"
) t
ORDER BY "file_count" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```
