Begin Exploring Related Columns
Column name: potential usage  
• "path": location of each file; used to ① identify the file‑name extension (.py, .c, .ipynb, .java, .js) and ② measure directory depth by counting “/”.  
• "repo_name": optional filter in case we want to restrict to particular repositories (not strictly needed for the task).  
• Other columns ("mode", "id", "ref", "symlink_target") are not essential to count file‑types vs. depth.

Conditions that may be used  
• Directory depth > 10 →  ( LENGTH("path")‑LENGTH(REPLACE("path", '/', '')) ) > 10  
• Extension match →  "path" ILIKE '%.py'  (similar for .c, .ipynb, .java, .js)

Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL queries (each ends with LIMIT 20) growing from simple inspection to a final aggregation that could answer the original question.

```sql
-- Description: 1) Quick look at a handful of file paths in the sample to understand the data.
SELECT 
  "repo_name",
  "path"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_FILES"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 2) Show distinct file‑name extensions that exist in the sample.
SELECT DISTINCT
  SPLIT_PART("path", '.', -1) AS "extension"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_FILES"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 3) For a few rows, display directory depth (slash count) beside each path.
SELECT 
  "path",
  ( LENGTH("path") - LENGTH(REPLACE("path", '/', '')) )  AS "dir_depth"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_FILES"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 4) Peek at Python files whose directory depth is already > 10.
SELECT 
  "path"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_FILES"
WHERE "path" ILIKE '%.py'
  AND ( LENGTH("path") - LENGTH(REPLACE("path", '/', '')) ) > 10
LIMIT 20;
```

